Title: FlareUI quest tracker hook points for Questie data (used by the FlareQuestie overlay)
Why: FlareUI's tracker only knows what Blizzard's API tells it, and on Forever that is thin: quest POI distances are missing for most quests (Sort By Distance does nothing), classic quest items aren't "special" items (no item buttons), finished quests just say "Ready to turn in", and FlareUI has no Show on Map since 7.0.1. These are local functions, so a hook can't reach them. Each hunk adds one optional call (OT.Local*) that the FlareQuestie overlay fills from Questie's database; without the overlay every hunk falls through to FlareUI's own code. Alt-click on a quest is new: Show on Map.

=== FILE FlareUI\Modules\ObjectiveTracker.lua
--- OLD
local function Distance(questID)
    local distSq, onContinent = C_QuestLog.GetDistanceSqToQuest(questID)
--- NEW
local function Distance(questID)
    -- LOCAL FIX: a provider (FlareQuestie: Questie's spawn data, squared yards) answers first
    local provided = OT.LocalDistance and OT.LocalDistance(questID)
    if provided then return provided end
    local distSq, onContinent = C_QuestLog.GetDistanceSqToQuest(questID)
=== END

=== FILE FlareUI\Modules\ObjectiveTracker.lua
--- OLD
    elseif IsControlKeyDown() then
        ToggleFocus(questID)
--- NEW
    elseif IsAltKeyDown() then
        -- LOCAL FIX: Alt-click: Questie's map (FlareQuestie); FlareUI 7.0.1 dropped Show on Map
        if OT.LocalShowOnMap and not InCombatLockdown() then OT.LocalShowOnMap(questID) end
    elseif IsControlKeyDown() then
        ToggleFocus(questID)
=== END

=== FILE FlareUI\Modules\ObjectiveTracker.lua
--- OLD
        GameTooltip:SetQuestLogSpecialItem(self.logIndex)
--- NEW
        -- LOCAL FIX: an item from Questie's database has no quest log slot: its tooltip by item ID
        if self.localItemID then GameTooltip:SetItemByID(self.localItemID) else GameTooltip:SetQuestLogSpecialItem(self.logIndex) end
=== END

